Start with a point  $O$  and a red circle centered at  $O$  that doesn't intersect any circle.  


- Take a homothety at  $O$  till the new circle (color it blue) is tangent to some disk  $\odot(O_1)$  at a point  $P$ .
- Take a homothety at  $P$  till the new circle (color it green) is also tangent to some disk  $\odot(O_2)$ .
- Expand the green circle while keeping it tangent to  $\odot(O_1)$  and  $\odot(O_2)$  till it is tangent to a disk  $\odot(O_3)$ .

