No one has posted a complex bash and I think it's worth posting as it can be bashed in <1.5 pages. 
If  $O$  is the circumcentre of  $\triangle ABC$  then  $APON$  is cyclic with diameter  $AO$ . So we are done if we can show that  $F$  lies on the circle with diameter  $AO$ , i.e.  $FA\perp AO$ . 
Let  $(ABC)$  be the unit circle. We compute  $d$ : $\frac{d}{\overline{d}} = ab \implies \overline{d}=\frac{d}{ab}$  $\frac{a-d}{\frac{1}{a}-\overline{d}} = \frac{a-\frac{b+c}{2}}{\frac{1}{a}-\frac{b+c}{2bc}} = \frac{abc(2a-b-c}{2bc-ab-ac}$ Using  $\overline{d}=\frac{d}{ab}$ , we get $\frac{a-d}{b-d} = \frac{c(2a-b-c)}{2bc-ab-ac}
\implies d=\frac{(b+c)(bc-a^2)}{3bc-3ac+c^2-ab}
\implies b-d=\frac{(a-b)(ac+ab-2bc)}{3bc-3ac+c^2-ab}
\implies \frac{b-d}{\overline{b-d}}=\frac{ab(ac+ab-2bc)}{c(b+c-2a)}$ As  $f$  lies on  $bd$ , this last quantity equals  $\frac{f-b}{\overline{f}-\frac{1}{b}}=\frac{b(f-b)}{b\overline{f}-1}$ So  $fc^2(b+c-2a)-\overline{f}abc(ac+ab-2bc)=c(b+c)(bc-a^2)$ .      (1) $f$  also lies on  $ce$ , so the last equation is still true if  $b,c$  are swapped: $ fb^2(b+c-2a)-\overline{f}abc(ac+ab-2bc)=b(b+c)(bc-a^2)$ .             (2)
(1)-(2):  $f=\frac{(b+c)(bc-a^2)(c-b)}{c^2(b+c-2a)-b^2(b+c-2a)}=\frac{bc-a^2}{b+c-2a}$ .
So  $f-a=\frac{(a-b)(a-c)}{b+c-2a}$ . 
Thus  $\frac{f-a}{f-o}=\frac{(a-b)(a-c)}{bc-a^2} \in i\mathbb{R}$ , so we are done.

