Let  $AC =: b$  and  $AB =: c$  for ease of typesetting.  By Pitot on quadrilateral  $BMNC$ ,
\[
\frac c2 + \frac b2 = 12 + 6 = 18,
\]
ergo  $b + c = 36$ .  Furthermore, the incircle of  $\triangle ABC$  is also the  $A$ -excircle of  $\triangle AMN$ , so
\[
1 = XY = MY - NY = AM - AN = \frac c2 - \frac b2,
\]
ergo  $c - b = 2$ .  Solving this system yields  $\boxed{AB = 19\text{ and }AC = 17}$ .

