We now put forth a claim. 

\textbf{Claim.} In the ending position, where no one can either share or eat any more mangoes, the people who are stuck with mangoes will have exactly one mango each. 

\textit{Proof.} Note that if a person who is stuck has more than one mangoes, they must have at least two. Therefore, they can eat the mangoes, so they aren't stuck, contradiction. \hfill  $\square$ Furthermore, assign a value to each position around the circle in a following way - for position  $n,$  assign it a value of  $2^n.$  The values of each position, along with the position numbers, are shown below. The values are outside of the circle while the positions are inside. 

