Let  $\angle BCD = x$ **Claim :** $EFGH$  is a rectangle. **Proof :** $\angle DFC = 180 - (\angle FDC + \angle FCD) = 90$ . 
Similarly all other angles are  $90$ . Hence  $EFGH$  is a rectangle. 

\begin{align*}
&DE = AD \sin \tfrac{x}{2} 
&DF = DC \sin \tfrac x2 
&\Longrightarrow EF = \sin \tfrac x2 (DC - AD)
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&CG = BC \cos \tfrac x2
&CF = CD \cos \tfrac x2
&\Longrightarrow FG = \cos \tfrac x2(CD - BC)
\end{align*} $[EFGH] = EF \cdot FG = \sin \tfrac x2 \cos \tfrac x2 (BC - AB)^2 = \frac{\sin x}{2} \cdot (BC-AB)^2$  $[ABCD] = AB \cdot BC \cdot \sin x$ Hence
\begin{align*}
    &\frac{(BC - AB)^2}{BC \cdot AB} = 2 
    &\Longrightarrow \frac{BC}{AB} \cdot \frac{AB}{BC} = 4 
    &\Longrightarrow x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0
    &\Longrightarrow x = 2 \pm \sqrt{3}
\end{align*}

We only take the positive value here. $\boxed{\frac{AB}{BC} = 2 + \sqrt{3}}$

