The condition  $CH$  bisects  $AT$  is equivalent to saying that the infinity points along the directions  $CA, CB, CH, AT$  form a harmonic bundle in that order. Identify each infinity point with a line through  $A$ , and consider the transformation which rotates these lines by  $90^{\circ}$  and takes the isogonal of them in the angle  $BAC$ . This induces a projective map on the infinity points, which sends the above four directions to the directions corresponding  $CH, AO, AC, AH$  respectively. Project from  $A$  onto line  $CH$  to get that  $AO$  bisects  $CH$ .

