u_2 (A_{k-1}) - (k-1)} = 1$  then we can let  $d=1$  so that the insides of the square brackets are even, thus  $2^{
u_2 (A_{k})} \ge k.$  Else if  $2^{
u_2 (A_{k-1}) - (k-1)}$  is an even positive integer than set  $d=2$ , which yet again makes the insides of the square brackets even. Thus, the result is proven and in particular for  $k=1000$  as well.</details>

