We will prove two well known lemmas, of which will be use later.
\begin{lemma}
    In an acute  $\triangle ABC,$  let  $S_1, S_2, S_3$  denote the spheres with diameters  $BC,CA,$  and  $AB,$  respectively. Then  $S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3$  consists of two points,  $P$  and  $Q.$  In a right triangle,  $P=Q.$  In an obtuse triangle,  $S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3$  consists of nothing.
\end{lemma}
