        \end{align*}
would all be asleep. However, this is in contradiction to our initial assumption that at no point in time are  $6$  mathematicians all asleep. Therefore the statement that all  $5$  mathematicians from  $S_i$  are asleep when  $M_{5i + 1}$  falls asleep must be false, proving the claim.  $\square$ The claim then provides the following information:
