Place numbers from  $1$ - $6$  in some cells so the following criteria are satisfied: $1.$  A cell contains at most one number. Cells can be left empty. $2.$  For each cell containing a number  $N$  in the grid, exactly two other cells containing  $N$  are at a Manhattan distance of  $N.$  $3.$  For each cell containing a number  $N$  in the grid, no other cells containing  $N$  are at a Manhattan distance less than  $N.$ [asy]
