\begin{align}
    &\sum_{j=1}^{i}(-1)^{j+1}j\binom{i-1}{j-1}2^{n-i}\notag
    &= \sum_{j=1}^{i}(-1)^{j-1}j\binom{i-1}{j-1}2^{n-i}\notag
    &= \sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}(j+1)\binom{i-1}{j}2^{n-i}\notag
    &= 2^{n-i}\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}(j+1)\binom{i-1}{j}\notag
    &= 2^{n-i}\left[\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}\binom{i-1}{j}+\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}j\binom{i-1}{j}\right].
\end{align}
- $x_1$  has a coefficient  $2^{n-1}$  and  $x_2$  has a coefficient  $-2^{n-2}$ .
- Component  $\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}\binom{i-1}{j}$  is an alternating sum and difference of binomial coefficients, and it's a well-known result that it equals to 0 for  $i-1>0$ .
- Now, let's evaluate the component  $\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}j\binom{i-1}{j}$  for  $i-2>0$ .
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{j=0}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}j\binom{i-1}{j} &= \sum_{j=1}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}j\binom{i-1}{j} &&\text{as  $0\binom{i-1}{0}=0$ }
    &= \sum_{j=1}^{i-1}(-1)^{j}(i-1)\binom{i-2}{j-1}
    &&\text{by  $k\tbinom{n}{k}=n\tbinom{n-1}{k-1}$ }
    &= (i-1)\sum_{j=0}^{i-2}(-1)^{j-1}\binom{i-2}{j}&&\text{translation of index, and  $(-1)^{j+1}=(-1)^{j-1}$ }
    &= 0.&&\text{alternating sum and difference of binomial coefficients}
\end{align*}
- Thus, the whole sum equals to \[E[\text{indexed alternating sum of  $T$ }] = \frac{2^{n-1}x_1 - 2^{n-2}x_2}{2^{n}} = \boxed{\frac{2x_1-x_2}{4}}.\]
</details>

