It is well known that:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Each angle in an equilateral triangle is 60
    \item Angle sum in a triangle is 180
    \item In an equilateral triangle, the perpendicular bisector of a side is also the angle bisector of the angle opposing the side
    \item A quadrilateral is cyclic if and only if opposite angles sum to 180
    \item Inscribed angles pointing to the same arc are equal, and is also half of the central angle(also known as the inscribed angle theorem)
    \item In a circle containing  $A, B, C$ , if  $AB = AC,$  then  $A$  is the midpoint of either minor or major arc  $BC.$  
\end{enumerate}
We reference each one as fact \# where where \# is the number in this list. 

