{\bf{Lemma}}:  $PADE$  is cyclic if and only if  $\triangle EPQ$  is equilateral.

{\it Proof}: From earlier, it is known that  $\angle PBD = 30.$  Thus, we have that:
\begin{align*}
    & \triangle EPQ \text{ is equilateral } 
    \iff & \angle QPE = 60 \text{ by fact 1}
    \iff & \frac12\angle QPE = \angle PDE 
    \iff & PADE \text{ cyclic by fact 5 and }Q \text{ as the center}
\end{align*} 

Put together, the previous two lemmas finish our problem.

