My problem! This is the form of the problem statement I submitted:
<blockquote>
Quadrilaterals  $ABCD \sim A_1B_1C_1D_1 \sim A_2B_2C_2D_2$  lie in the plane such that
\[\overline{A_1B_2} \subset \overline{AB}, \: \overline{B_1C_2} \subset \overline{BC}, \: \overline{C_1D_2} \subset \overline{CD}, \text{ and } \overline{D_1A_2} \subset \overline{DA}.\]
Prove that  $\overline{AC} \cap \overline{BD}$ ,  $\overline{A_1C_1} \cap \overline{B_1D_1}$ , and  $\overline{A_2C_2} \cap \overline{B_2D_2}$  are collinear.
</blockquote>

<details><summary>Diagram</summary>[asy]
size(400);

real theta = 36;

path omega = circle((0, 0), 1);

pair O = (0, 0);
pair P = (sqrt(1 - 2 * sin(theta * pi/180)^2), 0);

pair A = dir(196.6);
pair B = intersectionpoints(A -- A+(P-A)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[0];
pair C = intersectionpoints(B -- B+(P-B)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[1];
pair D = intersectionpoints(C -- C+(P-C)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[1];

pair Q = extension(A, A+dir(D-A)*dir(36), C, C+dir(B-C)*dir(36));

pair A1 = 3/5*A + 2/5*B;
pair B1 = (B - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;
pair C1 = (C - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;
pair D1 = (D - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;

pair A2 = 4/5*A + 1/5*D;
pair B2 = (B - Q) * (A2 - Q) / (A - Q) + Q;
pair C2 = (C - Q) * (A2 - Q) / (A - Q) + Q;
pair D2 = (D - Q) * (A2 - Q) / (A - Q) + Q;

pair K = extension(A, P, B, Q);
pair L = extension(B, P, C, Q);
pair M = extension(C, P, D, Q);
pair N = extension(D, P, A, Q);

pair X = extension(A, C, B, D);
pair X1 = extension(A1, C1, B1, D1);
pair X2 = extension(A2, C2, B2, D2);

draw(A -- C ^^ B -- D, gray);
draw(A1 -- C1 ^^ B1 -- D1, gray);
draw(A2 -- C2 ^^ B2 -- D2, gray);

dot(" $A$ ", A, dir(A));
dot(" $B$ ", B, dir(B));
dot(" $C$ ", C, dir(C));
dot(" $D$ ", D, dir(D));

dot(" $A_1$ ", A1, dir(A+B));
dot(" $B_1$ ", B1, dir(B+C));
dot(" $C_1$ ", C1, dir(C+D));
dot(" $D_1$ ", D1, dir(D+A));

dot(" $A_2$ ", A2, dir(D+A));
dot(" $B_2$ ", B2, dir(A+B));
dot(" $C_2$ ", C2, dir(B+C));
dot(" $D_2$ ", D2, dir(C+D));

dot(X);
dot(X1);
dot(X2);
draw(4/3*X1 - 1/3*X2 --  4/3*X2 - 1/3*X1, dashed);

draw(A -- B -- C -- D -- cycle, linewidth(1));
draw(A1 -- B1 -- C1 -- D1 -- cycle);
draw(A2 -- B2 -- C2 -- D2 -- cycle);
[/asy]</details>

<details><summary>Solution</summary>Let  $P$  and  $Q$  be the centers of the spiral similarities from  $ABCD$  to  $A_1B_1C_1D_1$  and  $A_2B_2C_2D_2$ , respectively, so that
\[\angle PAB = \angle PBC = \angle PCD = \angle PDA = \theta\]
and
\[\angle QBA = \angle QCB = \angle QDC = \angle QAD = \theta';\]
note that  $P$  and  $Q$  lie inside quadrilateral  $ABCD$ . By the Law of Sines,
\begin{align*}
    1 &= \frac{\sin(\angle A - \theta)}{\sin \theta} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle B - \theta)}{\sin \theta} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle C - \theta)}{\sin \theta} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle D - \theta)}{\sin \theta} 
    &= \frac{\sin(\angle A - \theta')}{\sin \theta'} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle B - \theta')}{\sin \theta'} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle C - \theta')}{\sin \theta'} \cdot \frac{\sin(\angle D - \theta')}{\sin \theta'}
\end{align*}
so monotonicity on the function  $f(x)=\frac{\sin(t-x)}{\sin x}$  gives  $\theta'=\theta$ , as  $\theta$  and  $\theta'$  are both less than  $\min(\angle A, \angle B, \angle C, \angle D)$ .

[asy]
size(300);

real theta = 36;

path omega = circle((0, 0), 1);

pair O = (0, 0);
pair P = (sqrt(1 - 2 * sin(theta * pi/180)^2), 0);

pair A = dir(196.6);
pair B = intersectionpoints(A -- A+(P-A)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[0];
pair C = intersectionpoints(B -- B+(P-B)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[1];
pair D = intersectionpoints(C -- C+(P-C)*dir(theta)*10, omega)[1];

pair Q = extension(A, A+dir(D-A)*dir(36), C, C+dir(B-C)*dir(36));

pair A1 = 3/5*A + 2/5*B;
pair B1 = (B - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;
pair C1 = (C - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;
pair D1 = (D - P) * (A1 - P) / (A - P) + P;

pair A2 = 4/5*A + 1/5*D;
