Let  $B=(-1,0)$  and  $C=(1,0)$ . First, we derive a formula to compute the point  $Y$  such that  $X$  is the  $Y$ -excenter of  $YBC$ . Let  $X=(m,n)$ . The slope of  $BX$  is  $\frac n{m+1}$ , so by the tangent double angle formula, the slope of  $BY$  is  $\frac{2n(m+1)}{(m+1)^2-n^2}$ . Therefore,  $Y$  lies on the line  $$ y=\frac{2n(m+1)}{(m+1)^2-n^2}(x+1). $$   Similarly,   $$ y=\frac{2n(m-1)}{(m-1)^2-n^2}(x-1), $$   so
\begin{align*}
\frac{2n(m+1)}{(m+1)^2-n^2}(x+1)&=\frac{2n(m-1)}{(m-1)^2-n^2}(x-1)
(x+1)(m+1)((m-1)^2-n^2)&=(x-1)(m-1)((m+1)^2-n^2)
x(-2(m+1)(m-1)-2n^2)&=-2m(m+1)(m-1)+2mn^2
x&=\frac{m(m^2-n^2-1)}{m^2+n^2-1}.
\end{align*}
Therefore,   $$ Y=\left(\frac{m(m^2-n^2-1)}{m^2+n^2-1},\frac{2n(m-1)(m+1)}{m^2+n^2-1}\right). $$  Furthermore, the slope of line  $XY$  is  $$ \frac{2n(m-1)(m+1)-n(m^2+n^2-1)}{m(m^2-n^2-1)-m(m^2+n^2-1)}=-\frac{m^2-n^2-1}{mn}, $$   so the equation of line  $XY$  is  $$ y=-\frac{m^2-n^2-1}{2mn}x+\frac{m^2+n^2-1}{2n}. $$  Let  $I_A$  be the  $A$ -excenter of  $ABC$ . Then,  $I_P$  and  $I_Q$  are isogonal conjugates in  $I_ABC$ . Since  $AI_A$  passes through the circumcenter of  $I_ABC$ , the isogonal conjugate of the line through  $A$  perpendicular to  $AI_A$  in  $I_ABC$  is a circumconic of  $I_ABC$  that intersects the circumcircle at the reflection of  $I_A$  over the perpendicular bisector of  $BC$ . Also, the isogonal conjugate of  $A$  is the reflection of  $I_A$  over  $BC$ . Therefore, the circumconic has equation  $x^2+cy^2=1$  for some constant  $c$ . Then,  $I_P$  and  $I_Q$  are the intersections of the line and the circumconic.

Now, we will let  $X=I_A,I_P,I_Q$ . Then,  $m^2=1-cn^2$ , so the line  $XY$  has equation   $$ y=\frac{(c+1)n}{2m}x-\frac{c-1}2n. $$   This intersects  $BC$  at  $\left(\frac{(c-1)m}{c+1},0\right)$ . Let  $I_P=(p_1,p_2)$  and  $I_Q=(q_1,q_2)$ . Then,  $F$  satisfies   $$ y=\frac{(c+1)p_2}{2p_1}x-\frac{c-1}2p_2=\frac{(c+1)q_2}{2q_1}x-\frac{c-1}2q_2, $$   so   $$ x=\frac{(c-1)p_1q_1(p_2-q_2)}{(c+1)(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)} $$   and   $$ y=\frac{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}{2(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}. $$  Now, we compute the circumcenter of  $DEF$ . The three points on the circle are  $\left(\frac{(c-1)p_1}{c+1},0\right)$ ,  $\left(\frac{(c-1)q_1}{c+1},0\right)$ , and  $\left(\frac{(c-1)p_1q_1(p_2-q_2)}{(c+1)(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)},\frac{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}{2(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}\right)$ . The  $x$ -coordinate of the center is  $\frac{(c-1)(p_1+q_1)}{2(c+1)}$ , and the  $y$ -coordinate of the center is
\begin{align*}
&\frac{(c-1)^2}{2(c+1)^2}\left(\frac{p_1q_1(p_2-q_2)}{p_2q_1-p_1q_2}-p_1\right)\left(\frac{p_1q_1(p_2-q_2)}{p_2q_1-p_1q_2}-q_1\right)\frac{2(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}+\frac{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}{4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}
=&\frac{c-1}{2(c+1)^2}\frac{p_1q_2(p_1-q_1)}{p_2q_1-p_1q_2}\frac{q_1p_2(p_1-q_1)}{p_2q_1-p_1q_2}\frac{2(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}{p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}+\frac{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}{4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}
=&\frac{c-1}{(c+1)^2}\frac{p_1q_1(p_1-q_1)}{p_2q_1-p_1q_2}+\frac{(c-1)p_2q_2(p_1-q_1)}{4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}
=&\frac{c-1}{(c+1)^2}\frac{(p_1-q_1)(4p_1q_1+(c+1)^2p_2q_2)}{4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)}.
\end{align*}
The square of the radius of the circle is
\begin{align*}
&\frac{(c-1)^2}{(c+1)^4}\left(\frac{(p_1-q_1)^2(4p_1q_1+(c+1)^2p_2q_2)^2}{16(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2}+\frac{(p_1-q_1)^2(c+1)^2}4\right)
&=\frac{(c-1)^2(p_1-q_1)^2}{16(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(c+1)^4}\left((4p_1q_1+(c+1)^2p_2q_2)^2+4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(c+1)^2\right)
&=\frac{(c-1)^2(p_1-q_1)^2}{16(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(c+1)^4}\left(16p_1^2q_1^2+(c+1)^4p_2^2q_2^2+4p_2^2q_1^2(c+1)^2+4p_1^2q_2^2(c+1)^2\right)
&=\frac{(c-1)^2(p_1-q_1)^2}{16(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(c+1)^4}(4p_1^2+(c+1)^2p_2^2)(4q_1^2+(c+1)^2q_2^2)
&=\frac{(c-1)^2(p_1-q_1)^2}{16(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(c+1)^4}(4+(c-1)^2p_2^2)(4+(c-1)^2q_2^2)
\end{align*}

The circumcenter of  $BCI_A$  has  $x$ -coordinate  $0$  and  $y$ -coordinate  $\frac{a_2+\frac{a_1^2-1}{a_2}}2=\frac{1-c}2a_2$ . The square of the radius is  $$ \frac{(c-1)^2}4a_2^2+1=\frac{4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}4. $$  Let  $I_A=(a_1,a_2)$ . Then,  $A=\left(\frac{a_1(c+1)}{c-1},\frac{2ca_2}{c-1}\right)$ . The line through  $A$  perpendicular to  $AI_A$  has equation  $$ y=-\frac{2a_1}{(c+1)a_2}x+\frac{2a_1^2+2ca_2^2}{(c-1)a_2}=-\frac{2a_1}{(c+1)a_2}x+\frac2{(c-1)a_2}. $$   This intersects  $x^2+cy^2=1$  when
\begin{align*}
x^2+c\left(-\frac{2a_1}{(c+1)a_2}x+\frac2{(c-1)a_2}\right)^2&=1
x^2+\frac{4ca_1^2}{(c+1)^2a_2^2}x^2-\frac{8ca_1}{(c+1)(c-1)a_2^2}x+\frac{4c}{(c-1)^2a_2^2}&=1
\frac{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}{(c+1)^2a_2^2}x^2-\frac{8ca_1}{(c+1)(c-1)a_2^2}x+\frac{4c-(c-1)^2a_2^2}{(c-1)^2a_2^2}&=0
\frac{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}{(c+1)^2a_2^2}x^2-\frac{8ca_1}{(c+1)(c-1)a_2^2}x+\frac{4ca_1^2+(c+1)(3c-1)a_2^2}{(c-1)^2a_2^2}&=0.
\end{align*}

Additionally, the line also has equation  $x=-\frac{(c+1)a_2}{2a_1}y+\frac{c+1}{a_1(c-1)}$ . Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\left(-\frac{(c+1)a_2}{2a_1}y+\frac{c+1}{a_1(c-1)}\right)^2+cy^2&=1
\frac{(c+1)^2a_2^2}{4a_1^2}y^2+cy^2-\frac{(c+1)^2a_2}{a_1^2(c-1)}y+\frac{(c+1)^2}{a_1^2(c-1)^2}-1&=0
\frac{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}{4a_1^2}y^2-\frac{(c+1)^2a_2}{a_1^2(c-1)}y+\frac{4ca_1^2+c(c+1)^2a_2^2}{a_1^2(c-1)^2}&=0
(c-1)^2(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)y^2-4(c-1)(c+1)^2a_2y+4c(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)&=0.
\end{align*}

Now, we have
\begin{align*}
(4+(c-1)^2p_2^2)(4+(c-1)^2q_2^2)&=16+4(c-1)^2(p_2+q_2)^2-8(c-1)^2p_2q_2+(c-1)^4p_2^2q_2^2
&=16+\frac{64(c+1)^4a_2^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}-\frac{32c(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}+\frac{16c^2(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=\frac{16(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2+64(c+1)^4a_2^2(a_1^2+ca_2^2)}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}+\frac{16c^2(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2-32c(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=16\frac{16c^2a_1^4+(4(c+1)^4+8c(c+1)^2)a_1^2a_2^2+(4c+1)(c+1)^4a_2^4}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}+\frac{16c^2(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2-32c(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=16(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)\frac{4c^2a_1^2+(4c+1)(c+1)^2a_2^2+c^2(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)-2c(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=\frac{16(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(c+1)^4a_2^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the square of the circumradius of  $DEF$  is   $$ \frac{(c-1)^2(p_1-q_1)^2(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)a_2^2}{(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)^2(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}. $$  Now, we have  $$ p_2q_1-p_1q_2=\left(-\frac{2a_1}{(c+1)a_2}p_1+\frac2{(c-1)a_2}\right)q_1-\left(-\frac{2a_1}{(c+1)a_2}q_1+\frac2{(c-1)a_2}\right)p_1=-\frac2{(c-1)a_2}(p_1-q_1). $$  Therefore, the circumradius of  $DEF$  is equal to  $$ \frac{(c-1)^2a_2^2}{2(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}\sqrt{4a_1^2+(c+1)a_2^2}. $$  Now, we compute the distance between the circumcenters of  $DEF$  and  $BCI_A$ . As  $\frac{p_1+q_1}2=\frac{4c(c+1)a_1}{(c-1)(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}$ , we get that the square of the difference of the  $x$ -coordinates is   $$ \frac{16c^2a_1^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}. $$   Also, we get that the  $y$ -coordinate of the circumcenter of  $DEF$  is equal to
\begin{align*}
\frac{(c-1)(p_1-q_1)(4p_1q_1+(c+1)^2p_2q_2)}{4(p_2q_1-p_1q_2)(c+1)^2}&=-\frac{a_2(c-1)^2(4p_1q_1+(c+1)^2p_2q_2)}{8(c+1)^2}
&=-\frac{a_2(c-1)^2}{8(c+1)^2}\left(\frac{4(4ca_1^2+(c+1)(3c-1)a_2^2)(c+1)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(c-1)^2}+\frac{4c(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(c+1)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(c-1)^2}\right)
&=-\frac{a_2}{2(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}(8ca_1^2+(c+1)(c^2+4c-1)a_2^2).
\end{align*}
As the  $y$ -coordinate of the circumcenter of  $BCI_A$  is equal to  $\frac{1-c}2a_2$ , the difference in  $y$ -coordinates is equal to
\begin{align*}
-\frac{a_2}{2(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)}(8ca_1^2+(c+1)(c^2+4c-1)a_2^2-\frac{1-c}2a_2&=\frac{a_2}2\frac{-(8ca_1^2+(c+1)(c^2+4c-1)a_2^2)+4c(c-1)a_1^2+(c+1)^2(c-1)a_2^2}{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}
&=2a_2c\frac{(c-3)a_1^2-(c+1)a_2^2}{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the square of the distance between the two circumcenters is equal to
\begin{align*}
\frac{16c^2a_1^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}+4a_2^2c^2\frac{((c-3)a_1^2-(c+1)a_2^2)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}&=\frac{16c^2a_1^2(a_1^2+ca_2^2)^2+4a_2^2c^2((c-3)a_1^2-(c+1)a_2^2)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=4c^2\frac{4a_1^6+(c^2+2c+9)a_1^4a_2^2+(2c^2+4c+6)a_1^2a_2^4+(c+1)^2a_2^6}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}
&=4c^2\frac{(4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)(a_1^2+a_2^2)^2}{(4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2)^2}.
\end{align*}

This means that the distance between the two circumcenters is   $$ \frac{2c(a_1^2+a_2^2)}{4ca_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}\sqrt{4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}. $$  Now, notice that the sum of this distance and the circumradius of  $DEF$  is equal to  $\frac12\sqrt{4a_1^2+(c+1)^2a_2^2}$ , which is exactly the circumradius of  $BCI_A$ . As  $BCII_A$  is cyclic, this means that the circumcircles of  $DEF$  and  $BIC$  are tangent.

