<details><summary>Solution F</summary>Without loss of generality, assume  $\overline{AD} \nparallel \overline{BC}$ , as this case holds by continuity. Let  $(BCY)$  meet  $\overline{AB}$  again at  $W$ , let  $(ADX)$  meet  $\overline{CD}$  again at  $Z$ , and let  $\overline{WZ}$  meet  $(ADX)$  and  $(BCY)$  again at  $R$  and  $S$ .
	[asy]
