Separate the points into three regions as shown above. Let the number of mines in the red, blue, and green regions be  $a,b,c$  respectively.


- If  $a=c=0$  then our first move can be either up or right. After either of these moves we have at least  $2^{n-1-|M|}$  ways to finish due to induction (there certainly exists at least one way to finish), hence at least  $2^{n-|M|}$  paths total.
- If  $a=0$  and  $c>0$  then consider moving to  $(0,1)$ . There certainly exists at least one way to finish, hence by induction we have at least  $2^{n-1-b} \ge 2^{n-|M|}$  ways to finish.
- The case  $a>0$  and  $c=0$  is identical to the above.
- If  $a>0$  and  $c>0$ , then we're given there's at least one valid path -- WLOG its first move is to  $(0,1)$ . Then by induction there are at least  $2^{n-1-a-b} \ge 2^{n-|M|}$  ways to finish.

