as desired.**<span style="color:#f00">Claim</span>**:  $A, O_{BC}, O_A$  are collinear.**<span style="color:#00f">Proof</span>**: Consider the homothety that map   $$ X_A \rightarrow B, Y_A \rightarrow C $$  This also map   $$ O_A \rightarrow O_{BC} $$   this yields the claim.**<span style="color:#f00">Claim</span>**:  $AO_{BC}, BO_{AC}, C_{AB}$  concurrent.**<span style="color:#00f">Proof</span>**: Note that  $AX, BY, CZ$  concurrent at  $N$ .
Consider the inversion of  $X$ , which is  $O_{BC}$ Let  $M_A, M_A’$  be midarc not containing  $A$  and containing  $A$  of  $BC$ , respectively.
Note that   $$ (X, O_{BC} ; M_A, M_A’) = -1 $$  And since,  $\angle M_AAM_A’ = 90^{\circ}$ ,  $AM_A$  bisect  $\angle XAO_{BC}$ Thus,  $AO_{BC}$  pass through the isogonal conjuagte of  $N$ .
Hence,  $AO_{BC}, BO_{AC}, C_{AB}$  concurrent at the isogonal conjugate of  $N$ .

By all the claim above, we get that the perpendicular bisector of  $OK_A, OK_B, OK_C$  concurrent.
That is  $K_A, K_B, K_C, O$  are concyclic.
