We claim the answer is  $Q=22$ .

Note that an arbitrary line  $\ell$  will divide a circle into at most two parts. As these parts are continuous and connected, one is red and other blue. Thus, assuming not all colors are the same, we define a *bounding pair*  $(i,j)$  to be integers  $1\leq i,j\leq n$  such that  $A_i,A_j$  are red but  $A_{i-1},A_{j+1}$  are blue.

